# Packages added to Omarchy's list for the SM-T715 (aarch64), one per line,
# "name  # why". A line is MANDATORY (the build fails when pacman cannot
# install it) unless the name starts with '?': best-effort packages are
# skipped when unavailable on aarch64 and listed in the MANIFEST.
# Adapted from omarchy-tab-s2/image/rootfs/packages.extra: every
# name of that list exists in the aarch64 repositories (out/package-audit.tsv);
# the modem, GPS and Waydroid entries are left out until their kernel side
# exists on arm64.

# --- Memory ---
zram-generator          # compressed swap in RAM (/etc/systemd/zram-generator.conf)

# --- Display and input ---
mesa                    # panfrost (Mali-T760) and the exynos kmsro loader
squeekboard             # on-screen keyboard for a touch-only device (touch layer P1)
hypridle                # idle timer: screen off after 2 min through t715-keys (t715-idle.service)

# --- Audio ---
pipewire-audio          # PipeWire's BlueZ SPA plugin (spa-0.2/bluez5): Bluetooth audio
pipewire-pulse          # the PulseAudio server on PipeWire
rtkit                   # realtime priority for PipeWire

# --- Camera (omacam): not yet: it needs the t715-camera kernel driver on arm64 ---
# gstreamer gst-plugins-base gst-plugins-good gst-plugins-ugly gst-plugin-pipewire

# --- Console tools: usbutils, htop, vim, iw and wireless-regdb are in packages.base ---

# --- Diagnostics (GPU and power checks over ssh) ---
glmark2                  # reproducible GLES load with --validate
mesa-utils               # eglinfo, es2_info
i2c-tools                # i2cget: read-only PMIC checks
busybox                  # devmem: read-only SoC register checks

# --- Best effort ---
iio-sensor-proxy         # the accelerometer's orientation, for t715-rotate
?firefox                 # next to Chromium, Omarchy's default browser

# --- Apps of omamobile-apps, left out with it ---
gnome-calculator
gnome-clocks
loupe                    # image viewer: screenshots

# --- Tiles and audio clients ---
wf-recorder              # the Screen record tile (omamobile-screenrecord)
pipewire-alsa            # ALSA-only clients go through PipeWire
